WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.970
Dammit. Where the hell is Lupin?

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.340
Do you think he could have left the city?

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.300
I have a hard time picturing 
him giving up on a score.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.690
Agreed.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.840
You ready to do this?

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.990
This is not the time for hesitation.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.370
Okay, let's go.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:48.000
<b>Let's Talk About First Loves</b>

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.260
Who's in charge here?

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.500
You're... Colonel Tseng?!

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.360
First Lieutenant Puton, 
18th Infantry Regiment, sir!

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.660
May I inquire who...

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.250
The future queen of Padar.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.990
My apologies, sir!

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.410
It's Princess Dolma.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.900
She must be feeling better.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:29.470
We're on our way to crown our new queen.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.160
The troops will accompany 
us as our security detail.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.290
Looks like we've picked up some 
friends on the way to the palace.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.600
It's all thanks to you.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.810
Because of the airship?

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:48.270
As soon as I saw the Shake Hands' dirigible, 
I sent up a drone with a smartphone attached.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.760
That allowed me to hack into 
the airship's internal network.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.290
They were using a dongle with a range 
of only ten meters to run their network,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.280
so they didn't bother making it secure.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.300
It was no big deal.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.800
That's where you're wrong.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:14.970
You're much more remarkable
than you realize, y'know.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.590
I'm remarkable?

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.300
You sure are.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.300
I'm starting to think I should 
have you on my crew.

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.350
Thank you...

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:29.820
Now, let's go steal ourselves a princess.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.710
You still haven't located the king?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.830
And what happened to the squad 
that went after Lupin?!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.850
Princess Dolma's coronation 
is nearly upon us!

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:46.330
Make sure the internet stays out of action.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.200
By order of the High Priest—

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:56.700
Don't shoot!

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.080
They made us do it!

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.360
We were hired by the Shake Hands
 Corporation to rescue you.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.270
Shake Hands?

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.840
They want you to get the country back online,

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.020
and make it so that every 
citizen has access to this URL.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.370
The king?

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.960
What's going on here?

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.480
<i>My dear citizens of Padar...</i>

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.240
<i>This is your 45th king, 
Rajahara Sinha, speaking.</i>

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.240
<i>Those of you out there, brandishing weapons... 
Do you realize who you are pointing them at?</i>

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.260
<i>Once more, I ask you all to consider that.</i>

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:40.130
<b>This started outta nowhere</b>

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>It's the king</b>

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.510
<b>I don't want to fight</b>

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.000
<i>Are your guns trained on 
your fellow Padarians?</i>

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:49.390
<b>This started outta nowhere</b>

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:49.390
<b>It's the king</b>

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:49.390
<b>I don't want to fight</b>

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.680
<b>What are we supposed to do? 
It's other Padarians who are shooting at us</b>

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.520
<b>So our only choice
 is to return fire?</b>

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.960
Damn it all! What in the 
world is going on here?

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.770
Like I told you, this is a civil war, sir!

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.750
Believe me, I noticed—

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.570
Fujiko?!

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.520
Zenigata?

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:09.300
You came all the way here just to nab Lupin?

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.630
Of course I did.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:13.340
I'd even wade into a war zone to track him down.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.550
That's <i>literally</i> what you're about to do!

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:19.290
Where's Lupin, Fujiko?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.460
I couldn't care less where he is.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.460
What exactly happened between you two?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.360
<i>Internet access has been re-established.</i>

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:34.720
<i>The enemy has breached our perimeter.</i>

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.740
What happened to the 18th Regiment?

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.760
They were supposed to be 
our first line of defense.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.430
Well... Apparently, the bulk 
of them are on the move.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:45.860
And why would that be?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.850
They're escorting Princess Dolma.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:51.820
Impossible! Dolma is in the west tower...

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.740
You clowns are living in the past!

00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:00.000
You think you need 
a country to have an army?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.600
"Nations" are way too slow 
at keeping with the times,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.250
and that's why half of them are 
about to be taken off the board.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:09.140
Enzo, is it true that half the nations 
of the world are going to vanish?

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.320
I mean... What about my country?

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.770
Don't worry so much.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.850
It's not just the number 
of countries that'll reduce.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:20.880
Crime, misinformation, inequality...

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.220
All of it will be less than 
half of what it is now.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.810
That would indeed be wonderful, but...

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.040
It <i>will</i> happen!

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.020
Our PeopleLog app is 
pushing the clock forward.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.860
And nations, economies, 
kings, even master thieves...

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.890
will become relics of the past!

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:41.600
It's looking like a significant 
number are siding with the king.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.380
So we have lost?

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.430
It's fifty-fifty right now.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.730
Either outcome is acceptable.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:53.380
In this land, it is said that, for any great 
reconciliation, a sacrificial yak is needed.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.890
Princess Dolma... do you intend to...

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:02.370
Father's reforms should pass 
with little resistance now.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:09.270
Princess Dolma. For your safety...

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.040
How long has this been here?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:38.340
When in a position of authority, 
it is wise to anticipate every eventuality.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.900
Good work. I want you all 
to stand guard out here.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:44.610
Yes, sir.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.070
This is an emergency. I need to get past.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.580
Yes, sir. Head on through.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.580
<i>Biometric authentication?</i>

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.080
What's wrong?

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.840
I'm sure you're aware that 
we can't open it for you...

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:21.350
So much for tradition! 
This security system is cutting edge.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.360
These biometric scanners
 are a real pain to get around.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.600
This is gonna take a while...

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:33.310
Run analysis on the estimated response 
for corneal reflex and pupil dilation.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.350
Let's go.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.540
That was a huge help, Amy.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.630
It's Ami.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.070
Hey, Lupin...

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:54.640
Why did you steal me when we first met?

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:59.740
Because I thought you were valuable 
enough to be worth the trouble.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.390
I'm valuable?

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:04.880
I figured you'd grow up 
to be one hell of a woman.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.550
And look at you now: 
how much cooler can you get?

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.900
You're sauntering into 
a civil war to bail out a friend.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.900
Well, she <i>is</i> the only one I have.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:20.320
Hey, I've only got two friends myself.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.450
I think.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.050
We have prepared your escape route.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:30.970
Escape?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.470
We have many devout
followers in the north.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:38.850
We will carry out Princess Dolma's
 coronation there.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.230
Custom dictates that we must 
hold the ceremony in the palace.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:46.000
And lest we forget, we do not have our
symbol of monarchy, the Bloody Teardrop.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.910
I wouldn't worry about that.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:53.330
Is this your idea of a joke? 
That's clearly a duplicate.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:56.190
As one might expect, 
our future queen has a sharp eye.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:59.690
The people, however, will 
never notice the difference.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.550
You would allow a forgery 
to be worn at a coronation?!

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:06.750
Are you trying to trample 
all over our country's customs?!

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.510
And you claim to champion tradition? 
What sort of High Priest are you?!

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:13.970
All you care about is 
seizing power for yourself!

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:19.980
Well, the genuine article 
is always preferable...

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:25.480
But I've prepared a stand-in for 
you as well, Princess Dolma.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.970
How despicable...

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:34.170
You wanna put that 
coronation on hold for a sec?

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.480
You!

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.720
Lupin III!

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:56.670
Hey there, High Priest. 
It's time for our thieving contest.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.010
What are you talking about?

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.660
Well, you're a thief, aren't you?

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.390
After all, you're trying to 
steal this country, right?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.270
What?

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.680
Come with us, Dolma.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:12.220
Ami?

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:15.680
Your place isn't with a creep like him.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:18.680
My, such harsh words...

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:24.210
You seem convinced you have some kind 
of advantage, but I assure you, you do not.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.560
You have leaped into the 
middle of your enemy's forces,

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.190
only to end up as a sacrificial yak.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.090
Stop this!

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:37.390
It is my duty to protect our future queen.

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.140
Lupin?

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:55.040
Traitor—

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.080
Took you long enough, Lupin.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.920
We were certain you would 
turn up here eventually.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.900
Hey, guys!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:14.130
We got tired of looking for you.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:16.410
So we decided to wait at the finish line.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.380
N-Now, hang on a minute, Lupin...

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:24.730
L-Let's make a deal.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:31.010
Once this country is under our control, 
I can give you any prize you want!

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:31.660
How about it?

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:32.360
Won't happen.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.280
You're a two-bit trickster.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.660
You'd need to be a proper villain.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.570
Otherwise, even if you took the reins, 
you'd never really be in control.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.540
Are you suggesting that also 
applies to the current king?

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.690
Well, just look at the mess they're in here.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:52.070
Gotta wonder whether there's anyone in this 
country who has the chops to be a real villain...

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:53.780
A villain...

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:58.050
Lupin, you're an international fugitive, yes?

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:01.370
In that case, why don't you 
consider operating out of Padar?

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:06.380
We can tear up our membership 
to the ICPO and offer you protection!

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.900
<i>You've only glimpsed the 
treasures Padar has to offer!</i>

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:13.370
<i>Seven types of gemstone! 
Solid gold necklaces!</i>

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.140
<i>And the women!</i>

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:20.410
<i>The women here are to die for. 
Graceful, innocent, and so affectionate!</i>

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:22.270
Is that really the High Priest talking?

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:29.130
Ling... Someone hacked and 
crashed one of our airships, right?

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.710
"Underworld."

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.310
They put their name out there on purpose...

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.300
Get a load of that!

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.290
Just who do you think you are?

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:42.420
Director Albert of the DCPJ...

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.490
What's your take on this?

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:48.800
The coup d'état has failed. 
As a result, the CIA is likely to pull out.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:52.520
A statement in favor of the king's plans 
for reconciliation won't raise any eyebrows.

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:53.760
Very good.

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:56.920
Draw up a statement for 
the foreign minister to sign.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:03.060
Trying to pull a heist in front of <i>him</i>...

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.490
What an idiot.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.140
You only have to tell me what you want, Lupin!

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:12.190
There are things individuals cannot 
accomplish that a state can make happen!

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:16.250
Whether that's a harem or 
a safe haven. Whatever you want!

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:22.410
Excellent timing! These intruders 
are here for Princess Dolma.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:23.920
Eliminate them at once—

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:24.950
High Priest, Your Excellency!

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.550
Was everything you just said true?

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.470
You were deceiving us all along?

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:32.070
Oh, no...

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.010
Oh, yes.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:37.720
You just spilled your guts 
on a live broadcast.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:41.390
Lupin... you... you wretch!

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.990
Your Excellency! Answer us!

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:45.420
Swear before the gods that you weren't lying!

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:45.990
Your Excellency!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.900
Please answer us, Your Excellency!

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:48.980
Your Excellency!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.000
Just stamp "The End" on that guy.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.490
And you, Princess Dolma! 
Have you also betrayed us?!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.890
Please answer us, Princess Dolma!

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:58.590
No! Dolma was—

00:14:58.590 --> 00:14:59.240
That's right.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.290
I was—

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:09.250
High Priest, as long as we still have 
the princess, the fight isn't over.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.310
Let's make our escape.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:11.250
Stop this, Mack!

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:13.850
The CIA has your back.

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:18.760
You men! If you want your princess 
to live, don't move a muscle!

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.030
Wait!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.400
You're not getting away!

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.280
Ugo!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.560
Are you all right, Princess?!

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:35.780
Don't go near him!

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.800
We will not let America infest our country!

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:41.490
Wait! All of you, this man was...

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.310
I don't care who answers my 
prayers... God or the Devil...

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:59.230
Just someone... please save this country...

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:02.780
Please! Save us!

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:17.320
Dolma...

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.820
The American dog has been put down!

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:25.700
<i>People of Padar, drop your weapons!</i>

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:29.700
<i>The reformers and the traditionalists 
are not our enemies!</i>

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.600
<i>The western superpowers who seek to devour 
our nation from within are our foes!</i>

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:36.090
Dolma...

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.090
You wretched little liar!

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.290
You were going to—

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:48.620
<i>Padar is united! There are 
no enemies within our borders!</i>

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.620
Put down your weapons, and join 
hands with your countrymen!

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:12.960
Looks like somebody's got the guts 
to become a villain, after all.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.260
That was pretty smooth back there, Princess.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.100
Though, I guess you'll soon be queen.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.050
Lupin III...

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:31.290
I will follow your advice, 
and become a ruthless she-devil.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:34.050
Sounds great! I just <i>love</i> bad girls!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:36.930
What happened to the other "bad girl," anyway?

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.380
Don't rain on my parade, man.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.850
I have never agreed with 
your taste in that regard.

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.020
Aw, pipe down.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.990
Having friends is a wonderful thing.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:50.950
You'll get the opportunity
to make plenty yourself.

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:52.010
Yes.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:55.000
I am sure I will.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:03.830
Dolma!

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.530
Dolma... Are you okay?

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.510
As I said...

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:11.590
I have found my resolve.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:12.700
Not about that.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:14.830
I mean...

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.080
About Mr. Mack.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:23.030
I will tell you a secret.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:24.020
Come closer.

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:28.060
He was actually my first love.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.040
Thank you for sharing that with me.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:39.050
To tell you the truth, I...

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:50.540
You two were having fun back there. 
What were you talking about?

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.560
Romance.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.210
Ah, to be young.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:56.580
Hey, Lupin...

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.180
Talking about love...

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:03.070
Lupin, I'm in love with you.

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:08.720
Look, Amy, the thing is...

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:14.200
After all, whenever I'm scared or anxious, 
I see your face in my head.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:19.950
Based on that, I can only conclude 
that I'm in love with you.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:23.680
I don't think love is something 
you can analyze logically...

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.540
When I become a better 
woman than Fujiko Mine,

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:28.170
I shall require an answer.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:29.820
Is that okay?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.450
All right. I'll be waiting.

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:41.050
You sure you don't want to arrest me?

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:43.070
What exactly happened 
between you and Lupin?

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.940
What's this? Thinking about 
getting a job in the gossip biz?

00:19:45.940 --> 00:19:47.720
It falls under the umbrella 
of the investigation.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:51.280
Well...

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.180
Just tell me, Lupin.

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:56.210
What am I to you, anyway?

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:59.470
Fujiko... You're my...

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:18.460
I'm taking the Bloody Teardrop.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:23.700
He stole away.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.660
Well, he <i>is</i> a thief, after all.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:27.970
What?

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:31.500
It's rude to laugh when you're having 
a serious conversation, y'know!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.510
Sorry...

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:35.580
You're a good guy, Zenigata.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.690
Well, I <i>am</i> a police officer.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:42.260
See you around. Thanks for yesterday!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:45.010
But how do you feel about him, Fujiko?!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:48.170
I hate the guy!

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:18.810
I am Goemon Ishikawa.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:21.670
On a stormy night, with the wind roaring 
and a rumble of thunder in the air,

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:25.810
a murder occurs in the 
darkness of an old castle.

00:22:25.810 --> 00:22:28.790
And the person playing
 detective is... you, Lupin?

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:30.700
A thief as a detective?

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:35.560
Very well. If you do not intend to steal anything, 
I assume you will not need our help.

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:37.960
You can solve this case on your own.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:41.730
Next time: Introducing 
Detective Jim Barnett III.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:44.950
<b>Introducing Detective Jim Barnett III</b>

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:44.220
Mysteries have never been my specialty.
